# Tabular ML Lab — Environment Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and edit as needed.

# ── App ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
APP_PORT=8501
APP_MEMORY_LIMIT=4g

# ── Who can reach the app ─────────────────────────────────────────
# There is no setting here, and that is deliberate. The app does not have
# logins of its own — your institution's single sign-on decides who gets in,
# by sitting in front of the container. See UNIVERSITY_DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
# Earlier versions of this file offered AUTH_MODE=proxy. Nothing in the app
# ever read it, so it looked like a lock and was not one. It is gone rather
# than left to mislead.

# ── LLM Backend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The environment sets the DEFAULT for every session; each person can still
# pick another backend in the app's sidebar. Keys set here stay on the server:
# the app reads them at call time and never shows or saves them.
#   ollama    — Ollama at OLLAMA_BASE_URL (the --profile ollama sidecar, or an
#               Ollama your institution already runs)
#   openai    — OpenAI with OPENAI_API_KEY, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint
#               (vLLM, an institutional gateway) when VLLM_BASE_URL is set —
#               no real key is needed then
#   anthropic — Anthropic with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   disabled  — no AI features; the buttons are not rendered at all
LLM_BACKEND=ollama
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://ollama:11434
# VLLM_BASE_URL=http://vllm-server:8000/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Ollama sidecar settings (only if using --profile ollama)
OLLAMA_PORT=11434
OLLAMA_MEMORY_LIMIT=8g

# To give the app more memory, raise APP_MEMORY_LIMIT above. (A COMPUTE_PROFILE
# setting used to live here; like AUTH_MODE, nothing read it.)
